WEBVTT

00:15:29.290 --> 00:15:31.156
They have two gorgeous 8 x 10 glossies

00:15:31.180 --> 00:15:33.201
of meaningful things to them, and we say,

00:15:33.225 --> 00:15:35.596
"Which one would you like to give up?"

00:15:35.620 --> 00:15:36.771
"I have to give one up?"

00:15:36.795 --> 00:15:39.907
"Yes, we need one as evidence
of the class project.

00:15:39.931 --> 00:15:42.549
So you have to give me one.
You have to make a choice.

00:15:42.573 --> 00:15:45.319
You get to keep one,
and I get to keep one."

00:15:45.343 --> 00:15:48.319
Now, there are two conditions
in this experiment.

00:15:48.343 --> 00:15:50.621
In one case, the students are told,

00:15:50.645 --> 00:15:53.001
"But you know,
if you want to change your mind,

00:15:53.025 --> 00:15:54.878
I'll always have the other one here,

00:15:54.902 --> 00:15:59.377
and in the next four days, before
I actually mail it to headquarters" --

00:15:59.401 --> 00:16:01.334
yeah, "headquarters" --